{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.trivial_satisfies","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.trivial_satisfies","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondLinear.lean#L109-L115","doc":"Sanity check on the reduction, on the trivial functional: both sides are\n`0`, for every `z` and `d`. This confirms `bondRule_iff_sigma_case` is\napplicable, not that any interesting trace satisfies the rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.trivialMarkovLinear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.trivialMarkovLinear","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondLinear.lean#L100-L107","doc":"The structure is inhabited: the zero functional is a `MarkovLinear`.\n\nPresent so `MarkovLinear` is demonstrably not an empty abstraction. It is a\n*witness of inhabitation only* — the zero functional satisfies the bond rule\ntrivially for every `z`, so it is evidence about the definition's\nwell-formedness and about nothing else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.tr_bond_of_sigma_case","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.tr_bond_of_sigma_case","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondLinear.lean#L91-L98","doc":"The `d`-family, written out: given the `σ_g` case, every bond letter's\ncontribution is `z + d`. A proton-proton bond (`d = 0`) contributes `z`; a\nneutron-neutron bond (`d = -h`) contributes `z - h`, which\n`QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondRule.markovZ_sub_h` identifies with `z (1/q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.bondRule_iff_sigma_case","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.bondRule_iff_sigma_case","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondLinear.lean#L76-L89","doc":"**The bond rule holds for all `d` iff it holds at `d = 0`.**\n\nThe `(z + d)` family collapses to one equation. `↤` is the direction that\nmatters: proving the single `σ_g` case yields the whole family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.tr_mul_add_smul_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.tr_mul_add_smul_one","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondLinear.lean#L66-L74","doc":"**Appending `d • 1` is linear.**\n\n`tr (x * (s + d • 1)) = tr (x * s) + d * tr x`, for any `x`, `s`, `d`. This is\nthe whole reason the bond rule has the shape `z + d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.MarkovLinear.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.MarkovLinear.tr","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondLinear.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The underlying functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.MarkovLinear.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.MarkovLinear.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondLinear.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.MarkovLinear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovBondLinear.MarkovLinear","kind":"structure","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MarkovBondLinear.lean#L56-L62","doc":"A linear functional on an `R`-algebra — the minimum a \"trace\" must be for\nthe reduction below. Deliberately *not* asked to be a trace in the\n`tr (a*b) = tr (b*a)` sense: the reduction does not need it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}